        "raw": "<p>While I do confess that I've listened to the character creation sessions of Sentinel Comics Live with a notepad to see if I could reverse engineer things enough to make basic characters, I don't think I'll get there.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>That said, I was thinking that it might be possible to use what we've got to make some characters, and that the easiest test case would be Young Legacy.&nbsp; Since she uses the same card deck as her dad, most of her sheet will be identical, and I'm not going to re-type his character sheet.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Hero Name: Legacy&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Alias: Pauline Felicia Parsons</p>\r\n<p>Background: Dynasty</p>\r\n<p>Archetype: Physical Powerhouse</p>\r\n<p>Power Source: Genetic</p>\r\n<p>Personality: Aspiring Leader&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Principle of the Hero: (as Legacy)</p>\r\n<p>Principle of the Inheritor: (During Roleplaying, it's important to reflect on the example set by previous Legacies.)</p>\r\n<p>Minor Twist: What lesson have you forgotten?&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Major Twist: By miss-applying an old lession to a new situation, how did you make things worse?&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Powers: Awareness d6, Flight d8, Strength d8, Vitality d8, Laser Vision d10&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Qualities: America's Newest d8, Close Combat d8, Communications d8, History d8</p>\r\n<p>{Moved a d8 from Qualities to Powers and juggled the names. You could probably make the arguement that it should be Laser Vision d8 &amp; Strength d10, but dang, but her Laser Vision is pretty brutal in the card game.}</p>\r\n<p>Abilities: Same with 2 exceptions.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Replace Galvanize with&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Inspiring Presence: Boost using Amercia's Newest. Apply that Bonus to all Attacks and Overcomes until the start of your next turn.</p>\r\n<p>Replace Principle of the Mentor with</p>\r\n<p>Principle of the Inheritor: Overcome a challenge similar to one previous Legacies have faced before. Use your Max die &amp; everyone gets a Hero Point.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>What do you think, sirs?&nbsp;</p>",
